{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"justjack420","id":"592252026226999306","is_bot":0,"username":"justjack420"},"author_id":"592252026226999306","channel_id":"747915249050583091","content":"The Pit- acts as both the law of the wastes and everyone's favorite pass time.\n-PvP downtime\n-Located in the center of the Market\n\nThe Market- open air market set up in front of the Factory entrance. Patrolled by Red Coats. \n-Entrance to The Factory\n-Access to most nonmagical items.\n\nThe Factory- massive building at the center of the Wastes. Can be seen from almost any point in the Wastes.\n-No access without sneaking in (High DC)\n-BBEG head quarters\n\nMain Port- primary port of entry to the Wastes. Often full of Red Coats. Main recruitment hub for Scrapper clans.\n-Located at real world ferry dock.\n-All goods are inspected by the Red Coats\n-Lots of Scrapper Recruiters here\n\nThe Heaps- broken into 4 sections (cardinal directions), the mounds are made of a seemingly endless see of trash, much of it not of this world or era.\n-The outlining mountain range of trash, scrapping and hunting missions here.\n\n\nStrange Obelisk- in one of the far corners of the wastes a large obsidian Obelisk stands. Remnants of strange rituals litter the grounds around it.\n-Possible resurrections here\n-The Afflicted, a group of Osiris Worshipping Uru and Gnolls\n \nSmuggler's Port- a secret port which Scrappers can smuggle goods into and out of the Wastes\n-Secondary entry, hidden from BBEG and Red Coats.","created_at":"2020-09-27T21:58:08.175000Z","edited_at":"2020-10-05T22:40:48.896000Z","id":"759896686146486293","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
